    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing across the entire monorepo. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Issues Fixed\n\n**1. `src/finetune/governance.test.js` - \"flags schema violations with descriptive errors\"**\n   - **Problem**: `APPROVAL_STATUSES` was undefined when trying to call `.join()` \n   - **Root cause**: The constants were only exported in the default export, not as named exports\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `finetune/index.js` while keeping the default export intact\n\n**2. `src/eval/index.test.js` - \"runs default evaluations\"**\n   - **Problem**: Expected toxicity score to be 1 but got 0\n   - **Root cause**: The `toxicityMetric` function had a different signature than the other metrics. When called with `(outputs, references)`, it was receiving the references array as the `bannedTerms` parameter, causing innocent words in the references to be treated as banned terms\n   - **Fix**: Changed `toxicityMetric` signature from `(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `(outputs, references)` to match the interface of other metrics, and hardcoded it to always use `defaultBannedTerms`\n\n**Test Results:**\n- \u2705 All 28 tests in frai-core passing\n- \u2705 All 11 tests in frai-gate passing  \n- \u2705 All existing public exports preserved",
